.TH AGENT-PS 1 "2026-10-02" "agent-tools 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
agent-ps \- list running coding agents and their working directories
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B agent-ps
[\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-cwd\-only\fR] [\fB\-\-tree\fR] [\fB\-\-kind\fR \fIKIND\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B agent-ps
lists running Claude Code and Codex processes with their working directory,
age, tty and tmux pane. Detection is process based, so the output reflects
what is actually running. Claude rows are enriched from the per-session
metadata under
.IR ~/.claude/sessions .
.PP
Codex runs as a node wrapper with a native child and helper processes;
these are collapsed to the top-level pid unless
.B \-\-tree
is given.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-json
Emit JSON instead of a table.
.TP
.B \-\-cwd\-only
Print unique working directories, one per line.
.TP
.B \-\-tree
Show wrapper and child processes instead of collapsing them.
.TP
.BI \-\-kind " KIND"
Only show agents of this kind
.RB ( claude " or " codex ).
May be repeated.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success; 1 when no agents are found (table mode only).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ps (1),
.BR tmux (1)
